From: programista-zacny <5969291+programista-zacny@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] netd: optional rule for directly-connected routes

Port of "netd: Allow devices to force-add directly-connected routes"
(LineageOS-UL android_system_netd 3f4551ad, a guarded revert of AOSP
92e8f96e) for the LTE build of the SM-T815: Samsung's legacy RIL sets
up the IPv4 address of rmnet0 itself, and without a rule that looks up
the main table (where the kernel put the directly-connected route) the
default route of the mobile network cannot be added:
  Error adding route 0.0.0.0/0 -> <gateway> rmnet0 to table 1002:
  Network is unreachable

LineageOS used the soong defaults needs_netd_direct_connect_rule_defaults
(TARGET_NEEDS_NETD_DIRECT_CONNECT_RULE), which vendor/lineage no longer
has; this uses the soong config variable netd.direct_connect_rule,
which only the LTE build sets. Without it nothing changes.
---
diff --git a/server/Android.bp b/server/Android.bp
index 44dc816..dffc4dc 100644
--- a/server/Android.bp
+++ b/server/Android.bp
@@ -42,6 +42,11 @@ cc_library_static {
         "netd_aidl_interface_lateststable_cpp_shared",
         "netd_defaults",
     ],
+    // gts210ltexx: soong config variable netd.direct_connect_rule, see RouteController.cpp.
+    cflags: select(soong_config_variable("netd", "direct_connect_rule"), {
+        true: ["-DNEEDS_NETD_DIRECT_CONNECT_RULE"],
+        default: [],
+    }),
     include_dirs: [
         "system/netd/include",
         "system/netd/server/binder",
diff --git a/server/RouteController.cpp b/server/RouteController.cpp
index 2f0e8e2..e607e5e 100644
--- a/server/RouteController.cpp
+++ b/server/RouteController.cpp
@@ -774,6 +774,26 @@ int RouteController::configureDummyNetwork() {
     return 0;
 }
 
+#ifdef NEEDS_NETD_DIRECT_CONNECT_RULE
+// Add a new rule to look up the 'main' table, with the same selectors as the "default network"
+// rule, but with a lower priority. We will never create routes in the main table; it should only be
+// used for directly-connected routes implicitly created by the kernel when adding IP addresses.
+// This is necessary, for example, when adding a route through a directly-connected gateway: in
+// order to add the route, there must already be a directly-connected route that covers the gateway.
+// (Legacy Samsung RILs configure the address of rmnet0 themselves; without this rule the default
+// route of the mobile network fails with "Network is unreachable".)
+[[nodiscard]] static int addDirectlyConnectedRule() {
+    Fwmark fwmark;
+    Fwmark mask;
+
+    fwmark.netId = NETID_UNSET;
+    mask.netId = FWMARK_NET_ID_MASK;
+
+    return modifyIpRule(RTM_NEWRULE, RULE_PRIORITY_DIRECTLY_CONNECTED, RT_TABLE_MAIN,
+                        fwmark.intValue, mask.intValue, IIF_NONE, OIF_NONE, UID_ROOT, UID_ROOT);
+}
+#endif
+
 // Add an explicit unreachable rule close to the end of the prioriy list to make it clear that
 // relying on the kernel-default "from all lookup main" rule at priority 32766 is not intended
 // behaviour. We do flush the kernel-default rules at startup, but having an explicit unreachable
@@ -1237,6 +1257,11 @@ int RouteController::Init(unsigned localNetId) {
     if (int ret = addLocalNetworkRules(localNetId)) {
         return ret;
     }
+#ifdef NEEDS_NETD_DIRECT_CONNECT_RULE
+    if (int ret = addDirectlyConnectedRule()) {
+        return ret;
+    }
+#endif
     if (int ret = addUnreachableRule()) {
         return ret;
     }
diff --git a/server/RouteController.h b/server/RouteController.h
index d8393e7..1d5e1dc 100644
--- a/server/RouteController.h
+++ b/server/RouteController.h
@@ -81,6 +81,9 @@ constexpr int32_t RULE_PRIORITY_UID_DEFAULT_NETWORK               = 29000;
 constexpr int32_t RULE_PRIORITY_UID_DEFAULT_UNREACHABLE           = 30000;
 constexpr int32_t RULE_PRIORITY_DEFAULT_NETWORK                   = 31000;
 constexpr int32_t RULE_PRIORITY_UNREACHABLE                       = 32000;
+#ifdef NEEDS_NETD_DIRECT_CONNECT_RULE
+constexpr int32_t RULE_PRIORITY_DIRECTLY_CONNECTED                = 30000;
+#endif
 // clang-format on
 
 class UidRanges;
